+
+<a id="ARCH-RECOVERY-001"></a>
+
+### ARCH-RECOVERY-001 — Last-known-good activation and degraded reads
+
+A D1 conditional lock row with holder, acquisition time, and expiry prevents overlapping Cron runs. The default `weather-sync` lock expires after 15 minutes so a crashed holder cannot block future runs indefinitely; release is owner-aware, and a second run aborts rather than proceeding concurrently.
+
+A candidate snapshot remains pending while its normalized weather, scores, rankings, and read models are validated. Activation is a D1 critical-state transition performed only after the complete candidate passes. A partial or corrupt candidate never replaces the previous active snapshot. Per-city failures are recorded and do not roll back unrelated valid city writes.
+
+Provider failure preserves the previous active snapshot. KV failure falls back to D1. A transient D1 read failure falls back to last-known-good KV or deployed static content. Returned stale data carries `stale: true` and its real `dataUpdatedAt`; no degraded result is described as live. If no trustworthy result exists, the use case returns an explicit unavailable outcome rather than contacting a provider.
+
+Roadmap: [REL-MVP-ARCH_RECOVERY_001](11-Roadmap.md#REL-MVP-ARCH_RECOVERY_001).
+
+#### Acceptance Criteria
+
+- Concurrent-run tests allow only one unexpired D1 lock holder and prove that an expired crashed lock can be recovered.
+- Fault-injection tests prove that an invalid candidate does not change the active snapshot pointer.
+- Provider, KV, D1, and partial-city failure tests produce the documented degraded outcome without a user-path provider call.
+- Stale results preserve the last trustworthy data, set `stale: true`, and expose the original update time.
+- Absence of trustworthy cached or persisted data produces a typed unavailable outcome, not fabricated data.
+
+## Rendering authority
+
+<!-- requirement
+id: ARCH-RENDER-001
